// `prec + 1` in parse_expression is the whole of left-associativity.
//
// The recursive call is made with the operator's own precedence *plus one*,
// so an operator of equal precedence waiting to the right fails the
// `prec < min_prec` test and is left for the loop. The loop runs again and
// hangs the new node above the old one, which leans the tree left.
main() : int {
    a : int = 10 - 4 - 3
    b : int = 100 / 10 / 2
    c : int = 1 + 2 + 3 + 4
    return a + b + c
}
